+## ADR-395 - Trace Smoothness, Optimize and automatic detection do what the dialog says (2026-09-25)
+
+**Status:** Accepted. | **Date:** 2026-09-25
+
+### Context
+
+The 2026-09-24 tracer audit (Finding 9) and its settings audit followed each Trace dialog control from
+its label to the code. This decision covers the outline finisher's curve controls, Line Art's
+automatic detection, the Enhance region re-trace and the preset definitions:
+
+- **Smoothness** set only the wobble flattener and arc evening. Loops measured from anti-aliased
+  pixels skip both, so the logo and the dragon traced byte-identically at 0, 0.83, 1 and 1.33 in
+  Line Art, Smooth and Edge Detection. On 1-bit art 0 to 0.83 did nothing, and Sharp's 0.55 sat in
+  that range, so Smooth and Sharp finished curves almost like Line Art (settings audit findings 1
+  and 9).
+- LightBurn's Smoothness runs from 0.0, which creates only lines, to 1.33, which creates only
+  curves [1], and its default of 1.0 is "generally a good starting point to produce smooth curves
+  without losing sharp corners" [2]. These are potrace's alphamax values: "If this parameter is 0, then no smoothing will be
+  performed and the output is a polygon. If this parameter is greater than 4/3, then all corners
+  are suppressed and the output is completely smooth" [3]. potrace scores each polygon vertex with
+  α = 4γ/3, rounds it if α < αmax and makes it a corner otherwise, and clamps α to 0.55–1 when it
+  places the curve [4].
+- **Optimize** 0 still merged boundary points into fewer vertices and curves. LightBurn documents
+  "0 means no merging" and a default of 0.2 [2] (finding 17).
+- Line Art's **Automatic (preserve pale details)** adds local-contrast detail only when the image
+  has colour: at least 32 pixels, and at least 0.2% of the image, non-white with channels 12 or
+  more apart. Pale grey detail was dropped and the operator could not tell (finding 5).
+- **Enhance region** decided the automatic (Otsu) threshold and that colour gate again on the boxed
+  crop, so the patched box could split ink from paper differently from the trace around it
+  (finding 11).
+- Every preset carried pathOmit, quadraticTolerance, blurRadius, blurDelta and lineFilter, which
+  only the multi-colour imagetracerjs path reads; no preset reaches it (finding 15).
+- 1-bit bars 4 and 8 px tall traced about 0.9 px too wide (X1). The dense-colour working grid above
+  1.5 MP was suspected of coarsening curve tolerances in source pixels (S1).
+
+### Decision
+
+1. **Smoothness is the corner control on every source** (`contour-smoothness.ts`,
+   `contour-corner-rounding.ts`), for the filled outlines and Edge Detection.
+   - At 1 the finisher keeps its own corners, and the output is unchanged.
+   - Below 1 each boundary loop is simplified to a 1 px polygon, and every vertex whose potrace alpha
+     reaches 4/3 × Smoothness becomes a corner. At 0 the outline is that polygon, drawn as straight
+     lines.
+   - Above 1 the finisher's corners whose alpha is below 4/3 × (Smoothness − 1) / 0.33 are released,
+     weakest first, all of them at 1.33. Each one is drawn the way potrace draws a curve vertex: one
+     cubic from a point on the edge before it to one on the edge after it, controls pulled toward
+     the vertex by its alpha clamped to 0.55–1. A curve reaches 0.45 of the shorter neighbouring
+     polygon edge and at most 8 source px, so a 12-point star keeps its points and a square keeps
+     its sides.
+   - The wobble flattener keeps its ramp, max(0, 6s − 5).
+2. **Optimize 0 is "no merging".** The merge tolerance is 0 there, and the finisher keeps every
+   measured boundary point with no simplification, spline resample or cubic fit. From 0 to 0.2 the
+   tolerance scale rises from 0.25 to 1; 0.25 is where fitted curves still carry fewer points than
+   the boundary they replace. At 0.2 and above nothing changes.
+3. **Preset values stay.** Sharp keeps Smoothness 0.55 and Optimize 0.15, which now give it more
+   corners and a tighter fit than Line Art. Smooth keeps Smoothness 1: every value above 1 scored
+   worse on both corpora.
+4. **The legacy tail's spline stays within the boundary it replaces**
+   (`contour-spline-envelope.ts`). Between two simplified vertices a resampled point may stand off
+   the chord no farther than the boundary does within 1 source px along the chord. Loops that end
+   in the least-squares fit (anti-aliased loops of 260 chain points or more) are unchanged; smaller
+   anti-aliased loops, such as glyphs, take the legacy tail and are held too.
+5. **Line Art keeps the colour gate, and the trace reports which path ran.**
+   `traceInkReport(image, options)` (`trace-ink-report.ts`) returns the path that decides ink
+   (`alpha`, `sketch`, `automatic-detail`, `faint-lines` or `brightness`), the brightness cut it
+   uses (a band, or a threshold with a flag when Otsu picked it) and, for Line Art, whether colour
+   was found. It follows `prepareTraceForContour`'s branch order and calls the trace's own gate and
+   threshold functions. It returns null for Edge Detection, Photo shading and the multi-colour path.
+6. **Enhance region uses the full source's verdicts.** `resolveRegionSourceOptions` decides the
+   colour gate (`resolveAutoSketchSource`) and the automatic threshold
+   (`automaticThresholdForTrace`) once on the whole image and carries them into the crop's trace as
+   `sourceAutoSketch` and `sourceOtsuThreshold`.
+7. **Presets drop the imagetracerjs-only fields.** They become optional in `TraceOptions`, and
+   `buildImageTracerOptions` leaves an absent field out, because imagetracerjs fills a default only
+   for a key that is missing.
+8. **S1 stays as it is.** The working grid keeps its tolerances in working pixels; converting them
+   to source pixels was measured and gains nothing (see Consequences).
+
+### Consequences
+
+- Line Art, Smooth and Edge Detection defaults are byte-identical to 85ee406 after decisions 1, 2
+  and 5 to 7 on the 12-image anti-aliased corpus, its 1-bit version, and the logo and dragon. Sharp
+  changes (Optimize commit: corpus IoU 0.9343 to 0.9370, nodes 15879 to 17064).
+- Smoothness now changes every kind of source. Drawn corners in Line Art at 0 / 0.3 / 0.6 / 0.83 /
+  1 / 1.33: 1838 / 712 / 371 / 260 / 243 / 76 on the anti-aliased corpus, 24484 / 12381 / 8695 /
+  7274 / 7189 / 1276 on the logo and dragon. potrace 1.16 at the same alphamax values on the
+  corpus: 1510 / 1151 / 859 / 699 / 553 / 455. Each step changes at least 4 of the 12 corpus
+  images and both real ones.
+- At 1.33 the wobble flattener runs at strength 2.98, and the 1-bit 12-point star crosses itself;
+  the topology repair then falls back to its pixel staircase, as it did before this decision.
+  Capping the flattener at strength 1 above Smoothness 1 fixes that shape and scored slightly
+  better on the 1-bit corpus (IoU 0.8907 against 0.8888 at 1.33), but it would remove the
+  ~3 px wobble erase that the ramp documents for rough scans, which these corpora do not test. It
+  is left for a decision with scanned sources.
+- X1: TODO_X1
+- Line Art's colour gate stays because opening it on greyscale art, which is what a luma
+  local-contrast gate would do on nearly every anti-aliased image, was measured to cost accuracy.
+  Forced on the greyscale corpus, the recovery moved IoU from 0.9576 to 0.8678 and mean edge error
+  from 0.086 to 0.375 px: its local cut sits above the anti-aliasing ramp, so text strokes widened
+  by 0.33 to 0.43 px and the thin-lines image by 0.73 px, and the noisy star gained a speckle loop
+  62 px from the shape. On the dragon it merged 1804 outlines into 1552. On a black disc beside a
+  pale grey bar and ring it does keep the pale detail when the image is clean, but grey noise with
+  a standard deviation of 24 levels adds 11 speckle loops, and 14 beside a disc with no pale
+  detail at all. TODO_GATE1BIT
+- Faint lines, the explicit option, recovers pale grey strokes 2 to 3 px wide but not an 8 px
+  bar. On the clean corpus it also widens thin strokes (IoU 0.8437 to 0.6618 on 16 px text, 0.9248
+  to 0.7195 on thin lines) and adds the noisy star's speckle loop, so it stays opt-in.
+- S1: on a tiled photograph traced by Line Art, the working grid holds 73, 61 and 49 points per
+  100 px of outline at 1.69, 2.56 and 4.19 MP, against 87 to 88 natively. Scaling the curve
+  tolerances to source pixels raised the point count by 4%, 9% and 19% and left the mean distance
+  to the native trace unchanged (0.315 to 0.315 px, 0.466 to 0.467, 0.625 to 0.637). The loss is
+  the smaller raster: 17%, 25% and 34% of the native outlines are missing.
+
+### References
+
+1. LightBurn 2.1, Trace Image reference: https://docs.lightburnsoftware.com/2.1/Reference/TraceImage/
+2. LightBurn legacy documentation, Tracing Images: https://docs.lightburnsoftware.com/legacy/Tools/TracingImages
+3. potrace(1) manual, `--alphamax`: https://potrace.sourceforge.net/potrace.1.html
+4. P. Selinger, "Potrace: a polygon-based tracing algorithm", 2003, section 2.3.3:
+   https://potrace.sourceforge.net/potrace.pdf
